WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:12.720
Hi everybody! I'm Josh Welsh, President of&nbsp;
Film Independent on what feels like day 3927&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.560
of being cooped up at home, I could&nbsp;
not be more excited to be here with you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:23.200
to share our nominations for the 2021 Film&nbsp;
Independent Spirit Awards. 2020 obviously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:28.000
was hell on earth but one glorious lifeline&nbsp;
these past few months has been the ability to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:34.640
watch so many great films and shows. This year's&nbsp;
spirit award nominees inspired us, connected us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:40.400
and have been a source of urgently needed light&nbsp;
in some pretty dark times, so even though we're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:45.360
all still stuck at home the time has arrived.&nbsp;
Let's come together and celebrate all the great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.840
work of 2020! Three new things to share with&nbsp;
you about this year's Spirit Awards, first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:54.800
we've introduced awards to recognize the best of&nbsp;
television that embodies the Independent Spirit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.320
the shows that we celebrate today possess the same&nbsp;
qualities original provocative subject matter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:06.160
uniqueness of vision and diversity that our film&nbsp;
nominations do. Second, at a time when the country&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:11.680
continues to undergo a serious reckoning with&nbsp;
racial justice Film Independent remains resolute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:17.120
in our commitment to fighting for a film industry&nbsp;
that looks like the world we actually live in! So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:21.200
when we talk about diversity and equity at&nbsp;
the Spirit Awards it's not an afterthought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.160
or a side note but a fundamental value that&nbsp;
runs through our entire process. This year of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:34.160
our nominated writers and directors 57 percent&nbsp;
are women and 48 percent are BIPOC and of our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:40.080
nominating committee members who worked so hard to&nbsp;
reach today's nominations, 67 percent were women&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:46.720
and 63 percent were BIPOC, third and finally this&nbsp;
year the spirit awards will be broadcast on IFC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:51.840
not on the Saturday afternoon before the oscars,&nbsp;
but on the Thursday night before the oscars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:58.000
Thursday April 22nd 10 pm eastern 7 p.m pacific,&nbsp;
one more note about the Spirit Awards for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:03.360
anyone who might be new to this. The winners of&nbsp;
the spirit awards are chosen by Film Independent&nbsp;&nbsp;

